== the prose runs: consecutive '' lines, as the parser read them ==
  (an ordinary ' line splits two runs; a string and a comment after code are not prose)
  lines 1-3
    | # Rates
    | 
    | Rates are **read** from the file.
  lines 5-6
    | - one
    |   - nested
  lines 9-9
    | Inside a function.
== the caret on code: every run is prose, a fold for each longer than a line ==
  doc-1 @1 markdown covers=true
  doc-5 @5 markdown covers=true
  doc-9 @9 markdown covers=true
  fold 1-3
  fold 5-6
  asked again, the same plan: true
== the caret moves into a run: that run is text again, and only that one ==
  onto line 5: reveal=true
  open run: 5   prose: doc-1, doc-9
  within it, to line 6: reveal=false
  out to code, line 8: reveal=true
  code to code, line 7: reveal=false
== a click on prose asks to edit it; a click on a result does not ==
  prose-edit doc-5 line 5
  block-none
  a link: block-none
  doc-1  collapsed, titled "Rates"
  doc-5
  doc-9
  and the plan moved: true
  pressed again: block-expanded
== a half-typed line that does not parse keeps the prose below it ==
  parses: false, runs still found: 3
  the plan: doc-1, doc-5, doc-10
  that line made an ordinary comment: doc-1, doc-5
== the setting ==
  shown: true, menu checked: true
  prose-off: 0 runs as prose, notice: documentation comments shown as comments
  sync_cursor never reveals with it off: false
  hand-edited "yes" reads as on: true
  toggled from there: prose-off
== a file that is not gBASIC has no prose ==
  entries: 0
